  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>When benzoic acid is heated with formic acid in presence of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Mno</mi></math>, benzaldehyde is obtained.</p><p>The reaction is given below, along with benzaldehyde, carbondioxide and water are also obtained.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mi>COOH</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>HCOOH</mi><munderover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>Heat</mi><mi>MnO</mi></munderover><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mi>CHO</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math></p>"
